{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385601-a-question-about-tenets","id":1385601,"title":"A question about Tenets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T07:26:14-07:00","id":1385601,"title":"A question about Tenets","content":"Is each chronicle intended to basically take place in an alternate timeline where every vampire in the world loses/maintains humanity based on the chronicle tenets? Or are tenets intended to be essentially group convictions, convictions everyone in the coterie shares because they have formed their own little sub-culture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T09:22:19-07:00","id":1385609,"title":"","content":"Tenets are in part 'general' morality for the whole chronicle, as well as in part genre emulation. Tenets are supposed to be set up as some basic guidelines of normal mentality for the game, and that is often based on the genre. A game based on the concept of John Wick is going to have different Tenets than a game based on Interview with the Vampire is going to have different Tenets than a game based on Underworld. Systematically, STs largely shouldn't care about Tenets and Convictions when it comes to NPCs and should more worry about them fitting the genre and narrative for the game.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what your'e getting at with 'every chronicle supposed to take place in an alternate timeline'. Like, are you talking about the effect it has on something written in a book? If so, that's largely the same as it always has been: NPCs and canon events, even in prior editions, rarely held to the exact minutiae of the rules in their plot advancements. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T09:48:20-07:00","id":1385613,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's a multiverse now. Like V:tR, in V5 each group have it own, particular universe.<br /> Like in comics, you have this dimension where vampires turn into wights for killing too many bad guys, and in another vampires turn into wight for treason on your coterie only. <br /> The rules that apply to pcs don't apply to the NPCS to show players how much more cooler the NPCs are than PCs. <br /> <br /> So, all you have to do whem STing V5 to your friends is ignore any rule when it comes to NPC: you decide if the npc have sucess or fail, and npcs dont gain stains no matter how severe the chronicle Tenets are, and in Chicago by Night they go further in separate NPC and PC mechanics to the point to not even put touchstones in all NPCs (despite being mandatory mechanics to PCs).<br /> <br /> Just create your own timeline with your group and have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:03:00-07:00","id":1385614,"title":"","content":"SPCs do not have to follow the tenets of your chronicle. only the PCs do. Tenets are basically the themes that your story will touch on. What is important to the story you are telling? They are the things that since they are important tot he story you are telling should be the things that your players are struggling with during that story.<br /> <br /> This is why they are listed in groupings with the overall theme listed such as gothic romance.<br /> <br /> There are thousands of moral complications that can be focused on but since this is a game we are only going to delve into these core tenets. Convictions also can be used to expand on the tenets of your story into the personal stories of your PCs by adding more things that could possibly give them stains. this is why the ST is given the option to give stains.<br /> <br /> This is a narrative game with many exceptions to the rules and the rules are truly just meant to be guidelines and not taken with such rigidity. So tenets don't apply to SPCs unless it is thematically appropriate for your story to do so. you don't have to track your SPCs humanity score.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:31:20-07:00","id":1385656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385601-a-question-about-tenets?p=1385613#post1385613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's a multiverse now. Like V:tR, in V5 each group have it own, particular universe.<br /> Like in comics, you have this dimension where vampires turn into wights for killing too many bad guys, and in another vampires turn into wight for treason on your coterie only.<br /> The rules that apply to pcs don't apply to the NPCS to show players how much more cooler the NPCs are than PCs.<br /> <br /> So, all you have to do whem STing V5 to your friends is ignore any rule when it comes to NPC: you decide if the npc have sucess or fail, and npcs dont gain stains no matter how severe the chronicle Tenets are, and in Chicago by Night they go further in separate NPC and PC mechanics to the point to not even put touchstones in all NPCs (despite being mandatory mechanics to PCs).<br /> <br /> Just create your own timeline with your group and have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You act like every bit of this wasn't how the narrative of Masquerade has always worked, where shit happens in the storyline that doesn't line up to how mechanics work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T17:35:59-07:00","id":1385693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385601-a-question-about-tenets?p=1385613#post1385613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's a multiverse now. Like V:tR, in V5 each group have it own, particular universe.<br /> Like in comics, you have this dimension where vampires turn into wights for killing too many bad guys, and in another vampires turn into wight for treason on your coterie only.<br /> The rules that apply to pcs don't apply to the NPCS to show players how much more cooler the NPCs are than PCs.<br /> <br /> So, all you have to do whem STing V5 to your friends is ignore any rule when it comes to NPC: you decide if the npc have sucess or fail, and npcs dont gain stains no matter how severe the chronicle Tenets are, and in Chicago by Night they go further in separate NPC and PC mechanics to the point to not even put touchstones in all NPCs (despite being mandatory mechanics to PCs).<br /> <br /> Just create your own timeline with your group and have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually called &quot;each ST runs their games their own way&quot; and has always been like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T07:11:49-07:00","id":1385817,"title":"","content":"While it's true that it's nothing new, it's kind of nice that the Developers bothered to throw this in as a way to say &quot;there's no wrong way to play this game&quot;. Too often I've witnessed angry debates in the past about the &quot;right way&quot; to play Vampire. I mean, somebody had to like Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, right? j/k","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}